# Events task changelog gate

**Changelog:** [`tasks/events/changelog.md`](../../../tasks/events/changelog.md)  
**Todo (canonical order):** [`tasks/events/todo.md`](../../../tasks/events/todo.md) — Cycle 1 venue chain B.1–B.7  
**Naming:** [`tasks/events/notes/1-notes.md`](../../../tasks/events/notes/1-notes.md) — `SAN-### · SPEC-ID — <full Linear title>`

## When this fires

Any Events (or Events-adjacent host/landing/detail) task that moves toward **In Review** or **Done** — including merges to `main`.

## Mandatory before Linear In Review / Done

1. **Append a changelog entry** (newest first) under `tasks/events/changelog.md`:
   - Full task name (never SAN-only)
   - PR #, commit SHA, branch, persona + surface
   - **Five dimension scores** (0–100) per rubric in changelog header
   - **Weighted % correct** and letter **grade** (A–F)
   - Evidence path when UI/agent touched
2. **Update the Summary table** at top of the same file (one row).
3. **Do not** flip Linear Done without user approval — stop at In Review with changelog + evidence linked.

## Scoring (must compute, not guess)

```text
% correct = round(0.25×spec + 0.25×tests + 0.20×review + 0.20×runtime + 0.10×process)
```

| Dimension | What proves the score |
|-----------|------------------------|
| Spec / AC | task-verifier probes; files match acceptance criteria |
| Tests | Vitest + Playwright pass counts; CI floor green |
| Review hygiene | cubic + CodeRabbit threads resolved at merge |
| Runtime proof | dev restart + Browser/Playwright; prod when shipped ([`mdeai-testing.mdc`](./mdeai-testing.mdc)) |
| Process | one issue = one PR; evidence file; full SAN title in PR/commit |

Use the **Template** section at bottom of `changelog.md` — copy, fill, do not skip dimensions.

**After append:** update **Grade**, **% correct**, and **Success rate** (= % correct) on the task row in [`tasks/events/todo.md`](../../../tasks/events/todo.md).

## Cycle 1 venue chain (must follow order in todo.md)

See Phase B in [`tasks/events/todo.md`](../../../tasks/events/todo.md). One PR per SAN-*; do not start B.1 until Phase A gate clears.

